Longtime leaker Sonny Dickson has <a href="https://x.com/SonnyDickson/status/2095058007415783801?s=20">shared an image</a> of differently colored SIM card trays that he claims are for Apple's upcoming iPhone 18 Pro models, suggesting Apple's flagship lineup will again be available in a trio of colors: Silver, Dark Cherry, and Sky Blue.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/sim-trays-iphone-18-pro-sonny-dickson@2x-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062056" /><br/>
Apple currently offers the iPhone 17 Pro in Cosmic Orange, Silver, and Deep Blue.<br/>
<br/>
Dickson shared the image in response to a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/01/iphone-18-pro-colors-include-black-but-skip-silver/"><em>MacRumors</em> report</a> on Tuesday covering a Chinese leaker's claim that the iPhone 18 Pro models could come in Dark Cherry, Sky Blue, and Black.<br/>
<br/>
Dickson told <em>MacRumors</em> the colors in the shared image are the only ones he's come across in recent months. However, the leaker did share iPhone 18 Pro dummy units <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/29/first-look-at-iphone-18-pro-color-options-revealed/">back in May</a> that included a fourth Black color. When that was pointed out to him, Dickson argued that black dummies are made every year, but it's not a color Apple prefers to use anymore. <br/>
<br/>
iPhone models sold in the U.S., Canada, and several other regions use eSIMs and don't come with SIM card trays, but devices sold in Europe, Japan, China, and Australia still include one (with the exception of the iPhone Air, which lacked a SIM tray everywhere it was sold).<br/>
<br/>
Chinese leaker Instant Digital in April said there would be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/02/iphone-18-pro-wont-come-in-black/">no black color for the iPhone 18 Pro</a>. Last year was the first time Apple's high-end iPhones have not been available with a black or dark gray color option in any way, so it's possible Apple will continue that trend. <em>Macworld</em> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/17/four-iphone-18-pro-colors-revealed/">reported</a> in the same month that Apple would offer Light Blue, Dark Cherry, Dark Gray, and Silver colors.<br/>
<br/>
